  "Ctrm": {
    "// Source": "CTRM for everyone in Production since the 2026-10-06 go-live: every contract and ticket read comes from the Scoular GraphQL API, no toggle. Rollback without a redeploy: App Service setting Ctrm__Source = ods (restarts the app; the switch re-reads config per call).",
    "Source": "ctrm",
    "// GraphQlUri": "The PRODUCTION gateway, reading production Db2 - NOT apiqa.scoular.com, which Dev and QA use and which serves a nonprod snapshot. A single POST to this exact path; no subscription key header (the API team confirmed none is expected). Rate limit for this identity: 3,000 calls per 60 s (raised from 1,000 by the API team on 2026-09-28, about 3x our worst case); a 429 carries Retry-After and X-RateLimit-Remaining.",
    "GraphQlUri": "https://api.scoular.com/internal/graphql",
    "TenantId": "1521f999-f722-4a4f-9747-166f93e9b0d1",
    "// ClientId": "App registration scoular-graphql-client-prod (service principal object id 06642509-1de5-4ebc-8e7f-a0342383f0d6), holding the Db2.Read.All role on scoular-graphql-api - the role contracts and tickets need. Dev/QA use scoular-graphql-client-nonprod (5e9cb280-b006-4705-9ecf-4bbf9d1c7085). Its client secret is what kv-orig-eus holds as Ctrm--ClientSecret.",
    "ClientId": "25ce2e75-76b6-4fb9-a6bf-ed76ef11adae",
